      {
        "id": "p19-q21-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $\\sqrt{4+2\\sqrt{3}}=1+\\sqrt{3}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Both sides are positive and their squares equal $4+2\\sqrt{3}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(1+\\sqrt{3})^2&=1+2\\sqrt{3}+3\\\\(1+\\sqrt{3})^2&=4+2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth $1+\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\sqrt{4+2\\sqrt{3}}$ are positive, so $\\sqrt{4+2\\sqrt{3}}=1+\\sqrt{3}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 27
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q21-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "If $x=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$, use part a to simplify $\\dfrac{1+\\sqrt{1+x}}{\\sqrt{1+x}}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt{3}$.\n\nUse part a to simplify $\\sqrt{1+x}$, then rationalise using the conjugate.",
          "worked": "Using part a,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{1+x}&=\\sqrt{1+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}\\\\\\sqrt{1+x}&=\\frac{\\sqrt{4+2\\sqrt{3}}}{2}\\\\\\sqrt{1+x}&=\\frac{1+\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1+\\sqrt{1+x}}{\\sqrt{1+x}}&=1+\\frac{2}{1+\\sqrt{3}}\\\\\\frac{1+\\sqrt{1+x}}{\\sqrt{1+x}}&=1+\\frac{2(\\sqrt{3}-1)}{(1+\\sqrt{3})(\\sqrt{3}-1)}\\\\\\frac{1+\\sqrt{1+x}}{\\sqrt{1+x}}&=1+\\frac{2(\\sqrt{3}-1)}{3-1}\\\\\\frac{1+\\sqrt{1+x}}{\\sqrt{1+x}}&=\\sqrt{3}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 66
      }
    ]
  },
